# FDD 26 review — "26 - Professional Learning - Sponsor" (Features 26.1-26.6).
# Ingested per abox/mied-v3/fdd-review/CONVENTIONS.md against the mied-v3 Professional
# Learning graph (proflearning-domain.ttl / proflearning-permissions.ttl /
# proflearning-api.ttl / proflearning-sequences.ttl, all loaded together), plus
# documents-api.ttl (agenda upload) and communications-api.ttl (not directly needed here
# — no email/notification story in this FDD maps to it the way FDD 28's Req_28_1_4 did).
#
# THIS IS THE ORIGINAL SOURCE of plrn:Question_SponsorApprovalWorkflowContradiction (Open
# Question #9), first raised during proflearning-domain.ttl's own v3 conversion FROM this
# FDD's submission-side description, and independently RE-confirmed from the opposite
# (admin/review) side by the just-completed 28-professional-learning-processing pass
# (see that file's Feature-28.1 header note and its own coverage-gap Annotation, which
# cites this FDD by name). This pass goes back to the actual source text and comment
# history behind that Question and REFINES it substantially — see the
# Question_SponsorApplicationGapRefined and Question_SponsorApplicationScopeWasContested
# Annotations below for what's new versus the original Question #9 wording. Net effect:
# Question #9's core claim (no SponsorApplication aggregate/entity/API exists anywhere,
# despite three independent sources — this FDD, FDD 28, and the domain model's own
# permission catalog — describing one) is CONFIRMED, not merely repeated; several new,
# more specific findings are added on top of it (see below).
#
# Structure of the document and what's used as the Requirement unit:
# - A "Business Specifications" prose section + an unnumbered "HIGH LEVEL SCENARIOS"
#   table (11 rows) restate the same sponsor/program-application/attendance narrative at
#   coarser grain — the HLS table is skipped per CONVENTIONS.md (duplicative).
# - An "Addendum" with real Feature/story numbering (26.1.1-26.1.6, 26.2.1-26.2.5,
#   26.3.1-26.3.2, [26.4 has no stories — see below], 26.5.1-26.5.5, 26.6.1-26.6.2) is
#   the primary Requirement unit used below — 21 items total. Unlike FDD 28's Addendum
#   (which had numbering collisions and several Business-Specification-only capabilities
#   never promoted to a number), this FDD's own Addendum numbering is clean and complete
#   — every Business Specifications topic maps to a numbered story, with no orphans and
#   no synthetic plrn:Req_26_BizSpec_* IDs needed.
# - Feature 26.4 ("Professional Learning Catalog") has no numbered stories at all — the
#   Addendum states outright, in prose, that "this feature is no longer considered
#   necessary." Modeled as a single rejected Requirement (Req_26_4), same treatment FDD
#   28's own Req_28_2 used for its mirror-image dependent feature (28.2, "Publishing the
#   Professional Learning Catalog" — FDD 28's own text explicitly cites THIS FDD's 26.4
#   as the reason it was dropped; the two rejections are two sides of the same decision,
#   cross-referenced below).
# - A genuine gap in the SOURCE MATERIAL, not this FDD's content: the pre-generated .md
#   sibling's extraction of story 26.5.2's Acceptance Criteria is BLANK (the heading
#   "Acceptance Criteria:" appears with nothing after it, immediately followed by
#   26.5.3). Direct inspection of word/document.xml found the real content was present
#   all along but wrapped in unaccepted w:ins tracked-change markup (Caswell, DTMB, three
#   inserted paragraphs dated 2026-03-11T20:14-20:15) that the .md extraction tool
#   evidently drops entirely — this is the ONLY place in the document where tracked
#   changes hide real, substantive content (checked systematically: only 4 w:ins blocks
#   exist in the whole document, three of which are these three 26.5.2 AC bullets; the
#   fourth is the "SCECH Eligibility" section for 26.2.1, already visible in the .md
#   because it was inserted as MODIFIED existing text rather than pure addition). The
#   real, current AC text is reconstructed and used for plrn:Req_26_5_2 below rather than
#   modeling it as empty or as a coverage gap that doesn't actually exist.
#
# Comments (26 total via comments.xml, several threaded across a Dec-2025-to-Mar-2026
# span with two distinct authoring generations — Ross/Dontje/Groom's Dec-2025/Jan-2026
# review round, then Caswell's Mar-2026 clarification-and-edit round responding to it):
# the single most load-bearing thread is on Feature 26.1 (Sponsor Application) itself —
# see Question_SponsorApplicationScopeWasContested below for the full timeline; it
# directly explains why proflearning-domain.ttl's own source domain doc still describes
# sponsor creation as EEM-only/external with no workflow, and materially refines Question
# #9's framing from "the FDD describes a workflow, the domain model doesn't have it" to
# "the workflow's very existence inside MiEdWorkforce was still an open, actively-
# discussed policy question during this FDD's own review, resolved only in Feb 2026,
# almost certainly after the domain conversion's own source document was last touched."
# Other comment threads, each folded into the relevant Requirement's own notes rather
# than given a separate Annotation where the resolution is clear-cut: comment 8 (Ross,
# renewal cadence confirmed annual, matches 26.2.3), comments 11/12 (approved-program
# stays searchable during re-approval, matches 26.2.5's own visible AC already), comments
# 13/14 (bulk-upload default-to-max confirmed, matches 26.5.1/26.5.2), comments 17/18/
# 19/223948687 (SCECH Eligibility section restructuring, resolved and reflected in the
# visible 26.2.1 AC text). Two threads ARE modeled as their own Annotations because they
# are NOT clearly resolved: the Feature 26.1 scope/login-model question above, and a
# field-level program-edit-approval nuance on 26.2.4/26.2.5 (comments 763087876/
# 377872980/1528602329 — see Question_FieldLevelReapprovalUnresolved below).
#
# Tracked changes: inspected exhaustively (see the 26.5.2 note above) rather than
# sampled, precisely because this document is the source of the FDD-defining Question #9
# and a stale-vs-corrected-text miss here would be costly; confirmed only the four
# w:ins blocks noted above exist, nothing else hidden.
#
# Wireframes: the Business Specifications prose names two inline: "Wireframe- Sponsor
# Program Application Wizard" and "Wireframe- Sponsor Program Application Management" (no
# numbered wireframe list like FDD 28's 14 captions — these two are the only explicit
# captions in this document). word/media holds 30 numbered image files (image1.png -
# image30.jpg) PLUS three more, image1a/1b/1c.jpg, embedded at package-root /media/ (a
# different relationship-ID range, rId257117023/451514264/707858046) rather than
# word/media/ — easy to miss with a media-folder-only listing, and exactly where they
# matter most: positioned directly inside story 26.1.1's own acceptance-criteria text
# (confirmed by document.xml position, not assumed), i.e. THE wireframe evidence for the
# single most contested feature in this FDD. Eleven images viewed and extracted (see
# Source documents below); the rest (image6-8, 10-12, 14-20, 22-24, 26-28, 30) were
# sampled by position per CONVENTIONS.md's depth-calibration guidance and confirmed
# consistent with the two clusters already captured (Program-application wizard/summary
# screens; Sponsor-facing attendance/roster/worklist screens) — no distinct undocumented
# feature area found among them.

@prefix sd:    <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:> .
@prefix oa:    <http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#> .
@prefix rdfs:  <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix plrn:  <urn:solutiondesign:instance:proflearning:> .
@prefix docs:  <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:> .

#################################################################
# Source documents
#################################################################

plrn:Fdd26Doc a sd:SourceDocument ;
    sd:docType "fdd" ;
    sd:section "functional-design-docs/26 - Professional Learning - Sponsor/26 - Professional Learning - Sponsor.docx" ;
    sd:notes "Covers Features 26.1-26.6 (document's own subtitle: 'Professional Learning - Sponsor (26.1-26.6)'). Authors Liz Breckel / Caitlin Groom / Beth Dontje; approved by Beth Dontje (MDE) and Caitlin Groom (CEPI), both 08/05/2025 per the signoff table — but comments.xml contains dated entries from 2025-12-04 through 2026-03-11, six-plus months after that signoff date (the same post-signoff-revision pattern already found in FDD 28's and FDD 29's own sibling documents), including tracked-change edits as recent as 2026-03-11 that are not yet reflected in the document's own approval table. This is the ORIGINAL source FDD for plrn:Question_SponsorApprovalWorkflowContradiction (Open Question #9) — see this file's header note." .

plrn:Wireframe1Doc a sd:SourceDocument ; sd:docType "wireframe" ;
    sd:section "abox/mied-v3/fdd-review/26-proflearning-sponsor/wireframes/wireframe-01-sponsor-application-landing.jpg" ;
    sd:notes "Confirmed by viewing: a 'Professional Learning' landing page with a single 'Become a Professional Learning Sponsor' card (placeholder 'Content to come...' body text) and an 'Application' button. Low-fidelity placeholder, not a functional wireframe of the application itself — but positioned exactly where story 26.1.1's own AC text sits in document.xml, confirming this is genuinely 26.1's own (thin) wireframe evidence, at package-root /media/ rather than word/media/ (easy to miss)." ;
    sd:definedIn plrn:Fdd26Doc .

plrn:Wireframe2Doc a sd:SourceDocument ; sd:docType "wireframe" ;
    sd:section "abox/mied-v3/fdd-review/26-proflearning-sponsor/wireframes/wireframe-02-sponsor-application-form.jpg" ;
    sd:notes "Confirmed by viewing: 'Sponsor Application, Step 1 of 4' with Entity/Contact-Information fields (Name, Phone, Email, MiLogin ID, reason for access requested) PLUS a 'Program Fee' and 'General SCECH Hours' field and a 'Program Documents' upload table — fields that belong to the PROGRAM application wizard (image2.png/image3.png, Wireframe-04 below), not a Sponsor application. This is internal wireframe-authoring evidence, not just a documentation gap: the Sponsor-application wireframe appears to be a copy-paste of the Program-application wizard template with only some labels changed, corroborating that Feature 26.1 received noticeably less design attention than Feature 26.2 — consistent with Question_SponsorApplicationScopeWasContested's finding that the feature's very existence inside MiEdWorkforce was still being decided during this document's review period." ;
    sd:definedIn plrn:Fdd26Doc .

plrn:Wireframe3Doc a sd:SourceDocument ; sd:docType "wireframe" ;
    sd:section "abox/mied-v3/fdd-review/26-proflearning-sponsor/wireframes/wireframe-03-user-authorization-reference.jpg" ;
    sd:notes "Confirmed by viewing: NOT a Sponsor-application screen at all — an 'Authorization and Security Agreement Instructions for State Continuing Education Clock Hours (SCECH)' access-request form with a View/Edit permissions-grant table (Teaching certificates worklist, Career and Technical Education Certificates Worklist, School Psychologist/Counselor/Administrator worklists, Manage demographics) and an 'Attestation for authorized representative' checkbox — this is MiEdWorkforce's existing IAM/User-Authorization access-request form (the same one cred:/iam: domains' own 'user authorization forms' concept refers to), reused here purely as a design ANALOGY for what a no-login-required intake experience should look and feel like, per 26.1.1's own AC ('similar to the user authorization forms'). Directly corroborates that 26.1.1 was deliberately modeled by analogy to an existing IAM flow rather than given its own original design — and that IAM flow itself has no counterpart SponsorApplication entity to extend." ;
    sd:definedIn plrn:Fdd26Doc .

plrn:Wireframe4Doc a sd:SourceDocument ; sd:docType "wireframe" ;
    sd:section "abox/mied-v3/fdd-review/26-proflearning-sponsor/wireframes/wireframe-04-program-application-wizard.png" ;
    sd:notes "Confirmed by viewing (this is the document's own explicitly-captioned 'Wireframe- Sponsor Program Application Wizard', word/media/image2.png — a filled-in example following the blank image1.png, both 'New program application, Step 1 of 4'): Sponsor information (read-only, pre-populated), Program type (dropdown + Display-in-catalog + 'Qualify program as' New-teacher/Re-certification checkboxes — the pre-restructuring layout comment 17/18 flagged for separation into 'SCECH Eligibility'), Basic information (name/category/subcategory/format/attendance-assurance), and an Endorsement(s) picker. Directly corroborates 26.2.1." ;
    sd:definedIn plrn:Fdd26Doc .

plrn:Wireframe5Doc a sd:SourceDocument ; sd:docType "wireframe" ;
    sd:section "abox/mied-v3/fdd-review/26-proflearning-sponsor/wireframes/wireframe-05-manage-applications-list.png" ;
    sd:notes "Confirmed by viewing (the document's own explicitly-captioned 'Wireframe- Sponsor Program Application Management', word/media/image4.png): a 'Professional learning applications / Manage applications' list with In-progress/All-applications tabs, an Advanced-search control, and a results table (Program name, Program #, Application #, Start/Submit date, Status: Review/Draft/Correct errors/Approved/Submitted) — the sponsor-facing analogue of plrn:Op_ListProgramApplications's admin-side list. Directly corroborates 26.2.3/26.2.4 (the '...' edit/renew affordance is implied by the row actions, not itself visible in this static capture)." ;
    sd:definedIn plrn:Fdd26Doc .

plrn:Wireframe6Doc a sd:SourceDocument ; sd:docType "wireframe" ;
    sd:section "abox/mied-v3/fdd-review/26-proflearning-sponsor/wireframes/wireframe-06-program-summary-attestation.jpg" ;
    sd:notes "Confirmed by viewing: 'New Program Application, Step 3 of 3' — a read-only Program Information / Program Documents / Program Dates & Locations summary followed by an 'Advisory' block and three attestation checkboxes ('I have read and understood...', 'I verify that the requirements...', 'I attest that the information submitted...') before a Submit button. Directly corroborates 26.2.2's summary-and-attestation review step." ;
    sd:definedIn plrn:Fdd26Doc .

plrn:Wireframe7Doc a sd:SourceDocument ; sd:docType "wireframe" ;
    sd:section "abox/mied-v3/fdd-review/26-proflearning-sponsor/wireframes/wireframe-07-document-upload.jpg" ;
    sd:notes "Confirmed by viewing: a document-upload modal (drag-and-drop or browse, 'Maximum file size 1MB', 'Files supported: .doc, .docx, or .pdf') actively displaying a rejected-file-type error ('One or more file types not supported. Please remove and try again.') on one of three listed files. Directly corroborates both 26.3.1 (upload) and 26.3.2 (enforced allowable file types) — the visible file-type list (.doc/.docx/.pdf) is a real, concrete detail neither the Addendum text nor proflearning-domain.ttl states explicitly anywhere." ;
    sd:definedIn plrn:Fdd26Doc .

plrn:Wireframe8Doc a sd:SourceDocument ; sd:docType "wireframe" ;
    sd:section "abox/mied-v3/fdd-review/26-proflearning-sponsor/wireframes/wireframe-08-add-attendee.jpg" ;
    sd:notes "Confirmed by viewing: an 'Add Attendee' modal with a 'Search by name or PIC' field and a Select-Attendee results table (Employee, UID, Certificate, Endorsement columns). Directly corroborates 26.5.1's online-entry path; the search field's generic framing (no organization/sponsor-scoping UI element visible) is consistent with the AC's explicit 'search globally for attendees since individuals may not be associated with the sponsor's entity' requirement, matching the already-documented gap on the API side (no /educators/search endpoint — see plrn:Req_26_5_1's own notes)." ;
    sd:definedIn plrn:Fdd26Doc .

plrn:Wireframe9Doc a sd:SourceDocument ; sd:docType "wireframe" ;
    sd:section "abox/mied-v3/fdd-review/26-proflearning-sponsor/wireframes/wireframe-09-edit-attendee-scech.jpg" ;
    sd:notes "Confirmed by viewing: an 'Edit Attendee' modal with an Attendance dropdown (showing 'Full Attendance'), a 'General SCECH Hours Awarded' numeric field (pre-filled 3.75, presumably the program max), and a Comment field, plus Remove/Save actions. Directly corroborates 26.5.2/26.5.3's award-adjustment stories — matches plrn:Op_AdjustScechAward's shape closely." ;
    sd:definedIn plrn:Fdd26Doc .

plrn:Wireframe10Doc a sd:SourceDocument ; sd:docType "wireframe" ;
    sd:section "abox/mied-v3/fdd-review/26-proflearning-sponsor/wireframes/wireframe-10-attendance-pending-approval.png" ;
