    sd:notes "Confirmed by viewing: 'Professional Learning Programs, Pending Applications' tab with a results table (Program Name, Application #, Start/Submit Date, Status: Info Required/In Review/Submitted) and a highlighted Program-Name hyperlink row. Positioned directly under the 26.6 Worklist text. Reads as a filtered view of the same Manage-Applications list (Wireframe5) rather than a functionally distinct worklist screen — no Sponsor-application action items appear anywhere in it, consistent with plrn:Req_26_6_1's own partial-gap note (Program-application worklist items only; Sponsor-application items have nothing to list, since no SponsorApplication entity exists)." ;
    sd:definedIn plrn:Fdd26Doc .

#################################################################
# Requirements — Feature 26.1: Sponsor Application
#
# GENUINE STRUCTURAL GAP shared by every story in this Feature — the ORIGINAL source of
# plrn:Question_SponsorApprovalWorkflowContradiction (Open Question #9). See this file's
# header note and the two Annotations following plrn:Req_26_1_6 for the full analysis;
# each story's own notes below cite the specific missing piece. satisfiedBy is left
# unasserted throughout this Feature — no SponsorApplication aggregate/entity/API exists
# anywhere in proflearning-domain.ttl/proflearning-api.ttl to point at, and
# plrn:Perm_SponsorApprove/plrn:Perm_SponsorDelete are themselves already documented as
# ungated stubs; linking them would overstate coverage that doesn't exist.
#################################################################

plrn:Req_26_1_1 a sd:UserStory ;
    sd:requirementId "26.1.1" ;
    sd:title "Complete initial Sponsor application form before full system access" ;
    sd:statement "As a new Professional Learning Sponsor, I want to complete an initial application form before I have full system access, so that I can officially apply to become an approved SCECH provider." ;
    sd:acceptanceCriteria "The system provides an initial SCECH Sponsor application form for new Professional Learning Sponsors to complete. The form must be accessible to users who have authenticated via MiLogin but do not yet have authorized user access to log into the MiEdWorkforce dashboard (similar to the user authorization forms). The system is aligned with the SCECH Sponsor Application Form structure, provided by business, and maintainable by the Professional Learning Admin. The application form must be completed prior to the sponsor gaining approval." ;
    sd:notes "THE root story of the SponsorApplication gap: no SponsorApplication aggregate/entity/API exists anywhere in proflearning-domain.ttl or proflearning-api.ttl to hold this form's data or lifecycle. Confirmed by Wireframe1/2/3 (plrn:Wireframe1Doc/2Doc/3Doc) — Wireframe3 shows this AC's own 'similar to the user authorization forms' language is a literal design reuse of MiEdWorkforce's existing IAM access-request screen, not a new original design. Also see Question_SponsorApplicationScopeWasContested: this story's own AC text ('authenticated via MiLogin but do not yet have authorized user access') describes a DIFFERENT access model than the comment thread's later resolution ('not require logging in to fill out and submit') — an unresolved discrepancy between the visible requirement text and the most recent stakeholder decision, not merely a missing implementation." ;
    sd:definedIn plrn:Fdd26Doc .

plrn:Req_26_1_2 a sd:UserStory ;
    sd:requirementId "26.1.2" ;
    sd:title "Name a Coordinator and/or Assistant Coordinator on the Sponsor application" ;
    sd:statement "As a Professional Learning Sponsor, I want to name a Coordinator and/or Assistant Coordinator on my application so that the state knows the designated contacts responsible for professional learning activities." ;
    sd:acceptanceCriteria "The initial application form includes a mandatory requirement to name a Coordinator. The initial application form includes a field to name an Assistant Coordinator." ;
    sd:notes "Same structural gap as 26.1.1 — no SponsorApplication to hold this data at intake time. Distinct from the ONGOING coordinator-management capability that IS modeled (plrn:CoordinatorAssignment entity on the already-approved plrn:ProfessionalLearningSponsorAggregate, plrn:CoordinatorAssignedEvent) — this story is specifically about capturing the Coordinator/Assistant Coordinator names as part of the initial APPLICATION, before any Sponsor record exists to assign them to." ;
    sd:definedIn plrn:Fdd26Doc .

plrn:Req_26_1_3 a sd:UserStory ;
    sd:requirementId "26.1.3" ;
    sd:title "Update Coordinator/Assistant Coordinator information after submission" ;
    sd:statement "As a Professional Learning Sponsor, I want to be able to update the Coordinator or Assistant Coordinator information after submission so that my profile accurately reflects my lead personnel." ;
    sd:acceptanceCriteria "The user can update the form details when a new Coordinator has been assigned. The user can update the form details when a new Assistant Coordinator has been assigned." ;
    sd:notes "Unlike 26.1.1/26.1.2, this story describes ONGOING maintenance (after the Sponsor is already approved), which is the scenario plrn:CoordinatorAssignment/plrn:ProfessionalLearningSponsorAggregate DO model conceptually — but the mechanism to actually perform this update is the same already-flagged gap plrn:Question_MissingSponsorSequences (Open Question #10) names: proflearning-sequences.md has no 'Manage Sponsor Contact Information' sequence despite the Sponsor aggregate's own 'Referenced In' list citing one, and plrn:Perm_SponsorEdit's own notes confirm no update-sponsor API operation exists at all. This FDD independently confirms that gap's real-world trigger (a Coordinator/Assistant Coordinator change) rather than raising a new one — see the Annotation immediately below." ;
    sd:definedIn plrn:Fdd26Doc .

[] a sd:Annotation ; oa:motivatedBy oa:reviewing ; sd:findingType "coverage-gap" ;
    rdfs:comment "Cross-reference, not a new finding: this story's own real-world trigger (Coordinator/Assistant Coordinator reassignment) is exactly the scenario plrn:Question_MissingSponsorSequences (proflearning-domain.ttl, Open Question #10) already names — no 'Manage Sponsor Contact Information' sequence exists in proflearning-sequences.ttl, and plrn:Perm_SponsorEdit has no backing API operation. Recorded here (rather than only in plrn:Req_26_1_3's own sd:notes) so this Requirement is not left unaccounted-for by the coverage-audit query." ;
    oa:hasTarget plrn:Req_26_1_3 ;
    sd:impact "M" ; sd:status "open" ; sd:definedIn plrn:Fdd26Doc .

plrn:Req_26_1_4 a sd:UserStory ;
    sd:requirementId "26.1.4" ;
    sd:title "Lock the application record and assign Pending Review status on submission" ;
    sd:statement "As a Professional Learning Sponsor, I want the system to lock the record after submission and assign a Pending Review status so that I know the application is officially under state review." ;
    sd:acceptanceCriteria "Upon submission for approval, the application status changes to Pending Review. The system locks the application record when the application is submitted for approval. The sponsor is prevented from making edits to the record while it is in the Pending Review status." ;
    sd:notes "No SponsorApplication status/lifecycle model exists anywhere — contrast with plrn:ApplicationReviewStatus (Submitted/PendingApproval/Approved/Rejected/RequiresInfo), the parallel, already-modeled status enum on the Program-application side. If a SponsorApplication entity is ever built, this status shape is the closest existing template to extend from, not a wholly new design." ;
    sd:definedIn plrn:Fdd26Doc .

plrn:Req_26_1_5 a sd:UserStory ;
    sd:requirementId "26.1.5" ;
    sd:title "Lead Administrator e-signature approval of the Sponsor application" ;
    sd:statement "As the Lead Administrator (Superintendent), I want to receive notification of a Sponsor Application and be able to electronically sign/approve it, so that I can authorize my organization's participation as a professional learning sponsor before the State reviews it." ;
    sd:acceptanceCriteria "Upon submission, the system identifies the Lead Admin and sends an email with a secure, one-time use link. The link directs the Lead Admin to a review page displaying applicant details and justification. The Lead Admin can Approve (requires E-signature/Attestation) or Deny (requires comments). If Denied, the workflow ends, and the application is not sent to the State. The system stores audit details of the action." ;
    sd:notes "The single largest, most specific piece of missing functionality in this Feature: a district-level Lead Administrator (Superintendent) e-signature gate, with its own actor (not 'Coordinator' or 'Professional Learning Admin' — a THIRD role never otherwise mentioned in proflearning-domain.md/proflearning-permissions.md), a secure one-time-use email link, and an audit trail — none of which has any counterpart anywhere in proflearning-domain.ttl, proflearning-permissions.ttl, or proflearning-api.ttl. No Role instance for 'Lead Administrator'/'Superintendent' exists in this domain's converted files at all. This is also the story most directly contradicted by proflearning-domain.ttl's Sponsor aggregate Design Note ('no PendingApproval state... sponsor creation is EEM-only') — see Question_SponsorApprovalWorkflowContradiction." ;
    sd:definedIn plrn:Fdd26Doc .

plrn:Req_26_1_6 a sd:UserStory ;
    sd:requirementId "26.1.6" ;
    sd:title "Route Sponsor Application to Professional Learning Admin worklist only after Lead Admin approval" ;
    sd:statement "As the MiEdWorkforce System, I want to route the Sponsor Application to the Professional Learning Administrator worklist only after Lead Administrator approval, so that State workers only review applications that have been authorized by the district." ;
    sd:acceptanceCriteria "The application status remains in a \"Pending Local Approval\" (or similar) state until the Lead Administrator completes the e-signature. Upon successful Lead Administrator approval, the application status changes to Pending Review and is routed to the Professional Learning Administrator's worklist. The Applicant (Sponsor User) receives a notification that their request has been approved by their Lead Admin and forwarded to the State." ;
    sd:notes "Depends entirely on 26.1.4/26.1.5's missing status model and Lead-Admin gate. Also the story FDD 28's own Feature-28.1 header note points at from the opposite direction: FDD 28 (Processing) independently confirms, via its own worklist/wireframes, that a Sponsor application DOES eventually reach the Professional Learning Admin's worklist — this story is the specific routing RULE (only after Lead Admin approval) that FDD 28 does not itself describe, since FDD 28 only sees the worklist from the point an item already appears in it." ;
    sd:definedIn plrn:Fdd26Doc .

[] a sd:Annotation ; oa:motivatedBy oa:reviewing ; sd:findingType "coverage-gap" ;
    rdfs:comment "Every one of Feature 26.1's six stories (26.1.1-26.1.6) depends on a SponsorApplication-shaped entity with its own status lifecycle (locked-on-submit / Pending Local Approval / Pending Review), a Lead Administrator (Superintendent) e-signature approval actor and gate, and Coordinator/Assistant-Coordinator capture at intake — none of which exists anywhere in proflearning-domain.ttl, proflearning-permissions.ttl, or proflearning-api.ttl. This IS the original source material for plrn:Question_SponsorApprovalWorkflowContradiction (Open Question #9, raised during proflearning-domain.ttl's own v3 conversion from this FDD's description) and is independently corroborated by 28-professional-learning-processing.ttl's own Feature-28.1 coverage-gap Annotation (the admin/review side of the exact same missing entity). Three independent sources — this FDD's submission side, FDD 28's admin/review side, and proflearning-permissions.ttl's own pre-existing proflearning.sponsor.approve/proflearning.sponsor.delete permissions — now confirm the same missing SponsorApplication aggregate (parallel in shape to the already-modeled plrn:ProgramApplication). High-impact, cross-cutting, and now triple-confirmed rather than merely asserted once." ;
    oa:hasTarget plrn:Req_26_1_1, plrn:Req_26_1_2, plrn:Req_26_1_4, plrn:Req_26_1_5, plrn:Req_26_1_6 ;
    sd:impact "H" ; sd:status "open" ; sd:definedIn plrn:Fdd26Doc .

plrn:Question_SponsorApplicationScopeWasContested a sd:Annotation ;
    oa:motivatedBy oa:questioning ;
    rdfs:comment "REFINEMENT of Question #9, not a restatement: this FDD's own comment thread on Feature 26.1 (anchored directly to the Business Specifications' first Sponsor-application bullet) shows the feature's very existence INSIDE MiEdWorkforce was still an open, evolving policy question well after the domain model was converted, which is the most likely explanation for why proflearning-domain.ttl's source doc still describes sponsor creation as EEM-only/external with no application workflow. Timeline, reconstructed from comments.xml: (1) comment 5 (Ross, DTMB-Contractor, 2025-12-04): 'It is my understanding this is currently taking place, external to MiEdWorkforce and still pending further discussion' — as of Dec 2025, the working assumption was that Sponsor-application intake happens OUTSIDE the system entirely, consistent with the domain doc's own Design Note. (2) comment 6 (Dontje, MDE, 2026-01-28): 'Yes, this needs further discussion as a group. This sponsor application should live in MiEdWorkforce but not require logging in to fill out and submit, similar to user authorization forms' — a PROPOSED reversal of that assumption, marked resolved (w15:done=1) despite saying discussion was still needed. (3) A new top-level comment, 1981370782 (Groom, CEPI, 2026-02-02, 'Per discussions 1/29'): 'The sponsor application should exist within MiEdWorkforce but not require logging in to fill out and submit, similar to user authorization forms, and require OEE approval, routed through the Professional Learning Worklist, included in 28.1' — the apparent FINAL resolution, roughly three weeks after comment 6, confirming in-app intake AND introducing a wholly new approval actor (OEE) never mentioned anywhere in the visible Addendum text (26.1.5/26.1.6 name only 'Lead Administrator (Superintendent)' and 'Professional Learning Administrator'). A second, separate discrepancy sits inside this same resolution: the 'not require logging in' language (comments 6, 1981370782) describes fully unauthenticated public submission, while 26.1.1's own visible AC text says the form 'must be accessible to users who have authenticated via MiLogin but do not yet have authorized user access' — authenticated-but-unauthorized, not unauthenticated. The visible Addendum text was never updated to match either the Feb-2026 login-model resolution or the newly-introduced OEE step. Any future SponsorApplication design needs to resolve both: which access model (26.1.1's text vs. the comment resolution), and where OEE fits relative to the Lead Administrator gate this FDD's own numbered stories already describe." ;
    oa:hasTarget plrn:Req_26_1_1, plrn:Req_26_1_5, plrn:Req_26_1_6 ;
    sd:impact "H" ; sd:status "open" ; sd:definedIn plrn:Fdd26Doc .

#################################################################
# Requirements — Feature 26.2: Program Application
#################################################################

plrn:Req_26_2_1 a sd:UserStory ;
    sd:requirementId "26.2.1" ;
    sd:title "Comprehensive application form to add a new Program" ;
    sd:statement "As a Professional Learning Sponsor, I want to access a comprehensive application form so that I can provide all necessary details to add a new program." ;
    sd:acceptanceCriteria "The system provides the SCECH Program Application form for submitting new professional learning programs. The application includes mandatory sections for Program Name, Program Type, Registration Link, Program Description, Category, Sub-Category, Program Fee, Maximum SCECH Hours, Purpose of Learning, and Program Agenda (via Program Documents Upload). The Program Type section requires selection of the Program Type from a drop-down list of values. The form allows the user to upload the Program Agenda document, with file types defined by the Professional Learning Admin. Upon selecting \"Next,\" the applicant will be prompted to enter the corresponding Program Dates and Location(s) for which they are applying." ;
    sd:satisfiedBy plrn:Op_SubmitProgramApplication, plrn:ProfessionalLearningProgramAggregate, plrn:Seq_ProgramApplicationSubmission ;
    sd:notes "Good match — every named field (name, type, registration link, description, category/subcategory, fee, max SCECH hours, agenda document, sessions/dates/locations) has a direct counterpart on plrn:ProfessionalLearningProgramAggregate's own value objects (ProgramContact/ProgramCategoryVO/ProgramFormatVO/SCECHAllocation/ProgramAgenda/ApprovalPeriod/SessionLocation). Confirmed by Wireframe4 (plrn:Wireframe4Doc). The tracked-change-inserted 'SCECH Eligibility' restructuring (comments 17/18/19/223948687 — splitting New-Teacher-PD/Re-certification indicators out of Program Type into their own section) is a form-layout refinement already reflected in the visible AC text above, not a modeling gap: it still maps to the same underlying fields." ;
    sd:definedIn plrn:Fdd26Doc .

plrn:Req_26_2_2 a sd:UserStory ;
    sd:requirementId "26.2.2" ;
    sd:title "Review summary and agree to attestations before submitting a Program application" ;
    sd:statement "As a Professional Learning Sponsor, I want to review a summary and agree to attestations before submission so that I can confirm the accuracy of the program details." ;
    sd:acceptanceCriteria "The system displays a summary of the application details before submission is allowed. The user is required to review the application details summary. The system displays attestation language for the user to review and agree with. The Professional Learning Sponsor must agree to the attestations prior to submitting the application form." ;
    sd:satisfiedBy plrn:Op_SubmitProgramApplication ;
    sd:notes "Confirmed by Wireframe6 (plrn:Wireframe6Doc, the document's own 'Step 3 of 3' summary+attestation screen). Same client-side-review treatment used elsewhere in this project's FDD reviews (e.g. FDD 28's Req_28_5_5/28_5_6): the summary display and attestation checkbox are UI-rendering concerns on top of the same submit operation, not a distinct backend capability requiring its own node — no attestation-acceptance field is separately modeled on plrn:ProgramApplication, which is a minor, low-impact documentation gap if attestation acceptance itself ever needs to be individually audited." ;
    sd:definedIn plrn:Fdd26Doc .

plrn:Req_26_2_3 a sd:UserStory ;
    sd:requirementId "26.2.3" ;
    sd:title "Renew existing approved Programs" ;
    sd:statement "As a Professional Learning Sponsor, I want to be able to renew my existing approved programs so that I can maintain current offerings and comply with academic year renewal requirements." ;
    sd:acceptanceCriteria "The application form allows the Professional Learning Sponsor to submit requests to renew existing programs. Selecting the \"...\" will allow the option to \"Renew Program\". The Professional Learning Sponsor can edit the application form details for existing programs. These fields will prepopulate with the prior academic year's information but can be modified as needed. Programs require renewal each academic year." ;
    sd:satisfiedBy plrn:Op_SubmitProgramApplication, plrn:ProgramApplication ;
    sd:notes "plrn:ProgramApplication's own description ('Entity tracking application lifecycle (new, modify, renew)') explicitly names 'renew' as a first-class lifecycle value, confirming this capability is modeled at the entity level — but plrn:Op_SubmitProgramApplication's own summary text only says 'Submit new or modified program application,' never mentioning renewal explicitly, and proflearning-api.ttl documents no distinct applicationType enum values anywhere for someone to confirm 'Renew' is actually accepted alongside 'New'/'Modify.' Minor documentation gap, not a structural one: the entity's own comment is good evidence renewal is intended to route through the same operation, just not confirmed by the operation's own documentation. Comment 8 (Ross, 2025-12-04, confirmed by Dontje's own resolution note) corroborates renewal happens 'every academic year' via 'the same [process] as adding a new application.'" ;
    sd:definedIn plrn:Fdd26Doc .

plrn:Req_26_2_4 a sd:UserStory ;
    sd:requirementId "26.2.4" ;
    sd:title "Modify existing approved Programs" ;
    sd:statement "As a Professional Learning Sponsor, I want to be able to modify my existing approved programs so that I can make necessary changes/modifications." ;
    sd:acceptanceCriteria "The application form allows the Professional Learning Sponsor to submit requests to modify existing programs. Selecting the \"...\" will allow the option to \"Edit Program\". The Professional Learning Sponsor can edit the application form details for existing programs." ;
    sd:satisfiedBy plrn:Op_SubmitProgramApplication, plrn:Rule_ModifiedProgramsRequireReapproval ;
    sd:notes "Clean match — plrn:Rule_ModifiedProgramsRequireReapproval's own text ('Sponsor-initiated edits... route through the full approval workflow') directly describes this story, applicationType=Modify per plrn:Perm_ProgramEdit's own notes. See Question_FieldLevelReapprovalUnresolved below for an unresolved refinement of exactly which fields trigger re-approval, raised by this FDD's own most recent (2026-03-11) comment thread." ;
    sd:definedIn plrn:Fdd26Doc .

plrn:Req_26_2_5 a sd:UserStory ;
    sd:requirementId "26.2.5" ;
    sd:title "Re-route a modified approved Program's application for approval" ;
    sd:statement "As a Professional Learning Sponsor, I want the system to re-route my modified application for approval if I change details of an already approved program so that the changes are reviewed by the Professional Learning Admin." ;
    sd:acceptanceCriteria "If changes are made to the program details after the program has been approved by the Professional Learning Administrator, the system automatically routes the updated application. The updated application is routed through the full Professional Learning Program approval process for review by the Professional Learning Admin." ;
    sd:satisfiedBy plrn:Rule_ModifiedProgramsRequireReapproval, plrn:Op_SubmitProgramApplication, plrn:ProgramModifiedEvent, plrn:Seq_AdminApprovesProgramApplication ;
    sd:notes "Strong match — plrn:Rule_ModifiedProgramsRequireReapproval, plrn:ProgramModifiedEvent, and the already-modeled admin-approval sequence together cover this end-to-end. Comments 11/12 (Ross/Dontje) already confirm, and the visible AC text already states, that the ORIGINALLY approved program details remain searchable while the modified application is under review — no separate modeling needed for that nuance, it's a read/query-time concern already satisfied by plrn:Op_GetProgram/plrn:Op_ListPrograms continuing to serve the prior approved version. See Question_FieldLevelReapprovalUnresolved immediately below for the one genuinely open nuance on this story." ;
    sd:definedIn plrn:Fdd26Doc .

plrn:Question_FieldLevelReapprovalUnresolved a sd:Annotation ;
    oa:motivatedBy oa:questioning ;
    rdfs:comment "A NEW, still-unresolved nuance on top of the already-modeled plrn:Rule_ModifiedProgramsRequireReapproval, from this FDD's most recent (2026-03-11) comment round: comment 763087876 (Groom, CEPI): 'After approval, all fields are editable. Upon submission if fields that require Admin approval have been edited, it is treated as a new application and sent for review/approval. If fields that do not require review are edited, the changes are immediately effective. (SOM team to verify which fields can be edited without review/approval).' This introduces a FIELD-LEVEL distinction (which specific fields trigger re-approval vs. take effect immediately) that plrn:Rule_ModifiedProgramsRequireReapproval does not currently express — the existing rule's only distinction is by ACTOR (sponsor-initiated edits always re-approve; admin edits never do), not by which field changed. The thread's own final exchange (comment 1528602329, Caswell, 2026-03-11 15:46, replying to Groom: 'Would you like to update requirement #5 to note that modifications will conditionally route for admin approval or become immediately effective based on the specific fields edited?') shows this was raised but not yet answered anywhere in the exported document — genuinely open, not merely undocumented. The visible 26.2.4/26.2.5 AC text was never updated to reflect it. Which specific fields require re-approval (per the comment's own 'SOM team to verify' caveat) is unknown outside this FDD's comment thread." ;
    oa:hasTarget plrn:Req_26_2_4, plrn:Req_26_2_5, plrn:Rule_ModifiedProgramsRequireReapproval ;
    sd:impact "M" ; sd:status "open" ; sd:definedIn plrn:Fdd26Doc .

#################################################################
# Requirements — Feature 26.3: Document Upload
#################################################################

plrn:Req_26_3_1 a sd:UserStory ;
    sd:requirementId "26.3.1" ;
    sd:title "Upload the Program Agenda document" ;
    sd:statement "As a Professional Learning Sponsor, I want to be able to upload my Program Agenda so that I can provide supporting documentation required for the application." ;
    sd:acceptanceCriteria "The SCECH Program Application includes a specific field for the Program Agenda (Document Upload). The Professional Learning Sponsor can successfully upload the required Program Agenda documentation as part of the application process." ;
    sd:satisfiedBy docs:Op_RequestDocumentUpload, plrn:ProgramAgenda, plrn:Seq_ProgramApplicationSubmission ;
    sd:notes "Clean match — plrn:ProgramAgenda is a real, modeled ValueObject and plrn:Seq_ProgramApplicationSubmission's own mermaid content already shows the coordinator's UI calling DocumentsAPI to upload the agenda before submitting the application. Confirmed by Wireframe7 (plrn:Wireframe7Doc)." ;
    sd:definedIn plrn:Fdd26Doc .

plrn:Req_26_3_2 a sd:UserStory ;
    sd:requirementId "26.3.2" ;
    sd:title "Enforce predefined allowable file types for document uploads" ;
    sd:statement "As a system, I want to enforce predefined allowable file types for document uploads so that data integrity and system security are maintained." ;
    sd:acceptanceCriteria "The system enforces a predefined list of allowable file types for the Program Agenda document upload. The specific allowable file types are defined and managed by the Professional Learning Admin (Reference Business Specification Professional Learning - Admin Users (14) for additional information). The system rejects uploads that do not conform to the predefined allowable file types." ;
    sd:notes "Confirmed by Wireframe7 (plrn:Wireframe7Doc), which shows a live 'File type not supported' rejection UI and a concrete allowed-type list (.doc/.docx/.pdf) not stated anywhere in proflearning-domain.ttl or the Addendum text itself. GAP: no admin-configurable allowed-file-type list exists anywhere in proflearning-domain.ttl/proflearning-api.ttl (this FDD's own AC explicitly defers ownership of that configuration to FDD 14, Professional Learning Admin, which was not reviewed as part of this pass) — this is a genuine cross-FDD dependency, not something this domain's own model would be expected to carry regardless. Documents domain itself (docs:Op_RequestDocumentUpload) was not inspected in full for this pass to confirm whether it has any generic file-type-restriction mechanism of its own; left unconfirmed rather than assumed. See the Annotation immediately below." ;
    sd:definedIn plrn:Fdd26Doc .

[] a sd:Annotation ; oa:motivatedBy oa:reviewing ; sd:findingType "coverage-gap" ;
    rdfs:comment "No admin-configurable allowed-file-type list for document uploads exists anywhere in proflearning-domain.ttl or proflearning-api.ttl, and this FDD's own text explicitly defers that configuration's ownership to FDD 14 (Professional Learning Admin), which was not reviewed as part of this pass — genuinely cross-FDD, not resolvable from proflearning's own source material alone. Wireframe7 (plrn:Wireframe7Doc) is concrete, real evidence the behavior is expected (a live file-type-rejection UI with a specific .doc/.docx/.pdf list), not merely a paraphrased AC." ;
    oa:hasTarget plrn:Req_26_3_2 ;
    sd:impact "L" ; sd:status "open" ; sd:definedIn plrn:Fdd26Doc .

#################################################################
# Requirement — Feature 26.4: Professional Learning Catalog (REJECTED, no numbered
# stories — the Addendum states outright, in prose, that the feature was dropped)
#################################################################

plrn:Req_26_4 a sd:Requirement ;
    sd:requirementId "26.4" ;
    sd:title "Professional Learning Catalog" ;
    sd:statement "It has been determined that this feature is no longer considered necessary." ;
    sd:notes "Not a user story — the Addendum states this feature's own removal in one sentence, no numbered sub-stories or acceptance criteria. This is the ORIGIN of the dependency FDD 28's own Req_28_2 cites: FDD 28's Feature 28.2 ('Publishing the Professional Learning Catalog') was dropped specifically BECAUSE this feature (26.4) was dropped first — FDD 28's own text says so explicitly ('Business Specification #26 Professional Learning - Sponsor, contains feature 26.4: Professional Learning Catalog which is considered no longer necessary'). The two rejections are two sides of one decision, not two independent ones. Consistent with plrn:Op_SearchCatalog's real, modeled 'catalog' actually being the PUBLIC catalog search surface (31.5 Public Search), a distinct capability from whatever Sponsor-side 'catalog' this dropped feature would have added." ;
    sd:definedIn plrn:Fdd26Doc .

[] a sd:Annotation ; oa:motivatedBy oa:reviewing ; sd:findingType "rejected" ;
    rdfs:comment "Feature 26.4 (Professional Learning Catalog) was explicitly dropped by the document's own authors. This is the origin decision that FDD 28's own Req_28_2/Feature-28.2 rejection is downstream of (see plrn:Req_26_4's own notes for the cross-reference). No action needed; nothing to build, nothing missing." ;
    oa:hasTarget plrn:Req_26_4 ; sd:status "resolved" ; sd:definedIn plrn:Fdd26Doc .

#################################################################
# Requirements — Feature 26.5: Awarding Professional Learning Hours
#################################################################

plrn:Req_26_5_1 a sd:UserStory ;
    sd:requirementId "26.5.1" ;
    sd:title "Add attendees to a program roster via online entry and file upload" ;
    sd:statement "As a Professional Learning Sponsor, I want to be able to add attendees to a program roster using both online entry and file upload so that I can efficiently manage participation records." ;
    sd:acceptanceCriteria "The Professional Learning Sponsor can add attendees to a program roster via online entry (manual input). The Professional Learning Sponsor can add attendees to a program roster via a file upload (bulk enrollment). The system allows the sponsor to search globally for attendees since individuals may not be associated with the sponsor's entity. The system includes a process for the SCECH Sponsor to upload bulk files for individual-level participation or attendance." ;
    sd:satisfiedBy plrn:Op_AddAttendee, plrn:Op_BulkUploadAttendees, plrn:Seq_AddAttendeesToProgram ;
    sd:notes "Both entry paths (online, bulk file) are real, modeled operations, confirmed by Wireframe8 (plrn:Wireframe8Doc). PARTIAL, already-documented gap on the 'search globally' requirement specifically: plrn:Seq_AddAttendeesToProgram's own SequenceReference for 'GET /educators/search?query={name}' is already marked resolutionStatus 'no-such-endpoint' in proflearning-sequences.ttl — this FDD's own AC ('search globally for attendees since individuals may not be associated with the sponsor's entity,' citing 'BRD 26.5.1' by name) is the actual source requirement that endpoint was meant to satisfy. Confirming, not raising, that gap." ;
    sd:definedIn plrn:Fdd26Doc .

plrn:Req_26_5_2 a sd:UserStory ;
    sd:requirementId "26.5.2" ;
    sd:title "Accept SCECH hours less than the program maximum" ;
    sd:statement "As a Professional Learning Sponsor, I want the system to accept SCECH hours less than the max amount so that I can report accurate SCECH attendance." ;
    sd:acceptanceCriteria "By default, the system applies the maximum approved SCECHs for the program as the awarded value for attendees. When utilizing the bulk upload function, the system allows the sponsor to define adjusted SCECH amounts in the data file prior to upload. The system will accept any value less than or equal to the maximum approved amount for each individual. After attendees are added (whether via bulk upload or single entry), the system provides the sponsor the ability to manually edit (increase or decrease) the awarded SCECH hours for any individual attendee within the UI, up to the maximum approved amount." ;
    sd:satisfiedBy plrn:Op_AdjustScechAward, plrn:Rule_DefaultScechEqualsMax ;
    sd:notes "SOURCE-MATERIAL NOTE: the pre-generated .md sibling shows this story's Acceptance Criteria as completely blank — the real text above was reconstructed from word/document.xml's tracked-change (w:ins, Caswell, DTMB-Contractor, 2026-03-11T20:14-20:15) content, which the .md extraction tool evidently drops; see this file's header note. Once reconstructed, this is a clean match: plrn:Rule_DefaultScechEqualsMax already states exactly this default-to-max-then-adjust behavior, and plrn:Op_AdjustScechAward is the real, modeled mechanism. Corroborated by comments 13/14/20/21/22 and their Mar-2026 replies (472884203/575263450), all converging on the same resolved behavior now reflected in the AC text used here." ;
    sd:definedIn plrn:Fdd26Doc .

plrn:Req_26_5_3 a sd:UserStory ;
    sd:requirementId "26.5.3" ;
    sd:title "Increase or decrease awarded SCECHs for a single attendee" ;
    sd:statement "As a Professional Learning Sponsor, I want to be able to increase or decrease awarded SCECHs for a single attendee so that I can accurately reflect partial attendance or non-completion." ;
    sd:acceptanceCriteria "The Professional Learning Sponsor can adjust the number of awarded SCECHs for a single attendee. The capability to increase or decrease awarded SCECHs is available, but not to exceed the max number." ;
    sd:satisfiedBy plrn:Op_AdjustScechAward ;
    sd:notes "Clean match, confirmed by Wireframe9 (plrn:Wireframe9Doc, the 'Edit Attendee' modal with its own SCECH-hours field). Same operation as 26.5.2, single-attendee framing." ;
    sd:definedIn plrn:Fdd26Doc .

plrn:Req_26_5_4 a sd:UserStory ;
    sd:requirementId "26.5.4" ;
    sd:title "Certify finalized program attendance" ;
    sd:statement "As a Professional Learning Sponsor, I want to certify the finalized program attendance so that the awarded SCECHs are officially processed and registered for the attendees." ;
    sd:acceptanceCriteria "The system requires the Professional Learning Sponsor to review attendee details before final certification. The system requires the Professional Learning Sponsor to agree to attestations prior to certifying attendance. The sponsor is able to certify the finalized program attendance. Upon certification, the individuals listed on the attendance roster are awarded the SCECHs approved by the sponsor." ;
    sd:satisfiedBy plrn:Op_CertifyAttendance, plrn:Seq_AdjustScechAwardsAndCertify, plrn:Rule_CertifiedAwardsImmutable, plrn:AttendanceCertifiedEvent ;
    sd:notes "Strong, end-to-end match confirmed by Wireframe10 (plrn:Wireframe10Doc). Attestation-before-certify is the same client-side-review treatment as 26.2.2 — no separate node needed. plrn:AttendanceCertifiedEvent's own consumers (Credentialing, Communications) already cover the 'attendees notified of new SCECHs' business-specifications text (a separate sentence in the prose, not its own numbered story)." ;
    sd:definedIn plrn:Fdd26Doc .

plrn:Req_26_5_5 a sd:UserStory ;
    sd:requirementId "26.5.5" ;
    sd:title "View and export a roster of attendees" ;
    sd:statement "As a Professional Learning Sponsor, I want the ability to create view and export a roster of attendees so that I can maintain external records or use the data for auditing purposes." ;
    sd:acceptanceCriteria "The system displays the roster of attendees for each program. The Professional Learning Sponsor can create and export the roster of attendees for external record keeping or auditing purposes. The ability to view the roster is tied to appropriate Professional Learning Sponsor permissions; the ability to export is tied to SOM UI/UX standards." ;
    sd:satisfiedBy plrn:Op_GetSessionRoster ;
    sd:notes "PARTIAL: view is a clean, already-modeled match (plrn:Op_GetSessionRoster, gated by plrn:Perm_AttendanceView). GAP: 'export' has no distinct API operation or mechanism anywhere in proflearning-api.ttl — the AC's own text defers export's shape to 'SOM UI/UX standards' rather than describing a specific format, consistent with this being a client-side rendering/download concern (e.g. a CSV/PDF export button over the same roster data) rather than a missing backend capability; still worth naming as a minor, low-impact documentation gap rather than silently assuming it's covered." ;
    sd:definedIn plrn:Fdd26Doc .

#################################################################
# Requirements — Feature 26.6: Worklist
#################################################################

plrn:Req_26_6_1 a sd:UserStory ;
    sd:requirementId "26.6.1" ;
    sd:title "Display a worklist of action items for the Sponsor" ;
    sd:statement "As a Professional Learning Sponsor, I want the system to display a worklist of action items so that I can quickly address tasks assigned to me." ;
    sd:acceptanceCriteria "The system provides a dedicated worklist interface for the Professional Learning Sponsor. The worklist displays action items requiring the sponsor's attention." ;
    sd:satisfiedBy plrn:Op_ListProgramApplications ;
    sd:notes "PARTIAL, mirroring FDD 28's own worklist-coverage pattern from the admin side: plrn:Op_ListProgramApplications already covers the Program-application half of this worklist ('Coordinators see only applications for their sponsor' per its own notes) — confirmed by Wireframe11 (plrn:Wireframe11Doc). The Business Specifications prose explicitly says this worklist 'will include sponsor and program applications that have action items assigned by the Professional Learning Processing Administrator (28.0)' — the SPONSOR-application half of that has nothing to list, since no SponsorApplication entity exists (Feature 26.1's gap). satisfiedBy still asserted since the Program-application half is real and the story is fundamentally about a worklist UI pattern already in place; the Sponsor-application half of the gap is the same one already captured under Feature 26.1, not re-raised as a separate Annotation here." ;
    sd:definedIn plrn:Fdd26Doc .

plrn:Req_26_6_2 a sd:UserStory ;
    sd:requirementId "26.6.2" ;
    sd:title "Worklist links directly to the application requiring action" ;
    sd:statement "As a Professional Learning Sponsor, I want the worklist to provide a link to the application so that I can easily navigate to the form requiring action." ;
    sd:acceptanceCriteria "The worklist allows the Professional Learning Sponsor to efficiently access the specific application (program or sponsor) associated with each action item. The system enables direct navigation from the worklist entry to the form or application details needing attention." ;
    sd:satisfiedBy plrn:Op_ListProgramApplications, plrn:Op_GetProgramApplication ;
    sd:notes "Same partial coverage as 26.6.1 — the hyperlink-to-detail UI pattern is confirmed by Wireframe11 (Program Name as a clickable link) and backed by the real list+detail operation pair for Program applications; the AC's own parenthetical '(program or sponsor)' again names the Sponsor-application half that has nothing to link to." ;
    sd:definedIn plrn:Fdd26Doc .
